     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On 7 January 2017 at 17:03, Terrence Jorgensen <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">tjorge...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><span><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>&#39;&#39;Error in (function (..., row.names = NULL, check.rows = FALSE, check.names = TRUE,  : arguments imply differing number of rows: 53, 0&#39;&#39;.</div></div></blockquote><div><br></div></span><div>Do you get the same error if you leave out the bootstrapping from your<font face=\"courier new, monospace\"> sem() </font>call?  Modification indices aren&#39;t going to utilize anything from bootstrap samples, so you don&#39;t need to request bootstrapping if you want to see them.  Also, to make sure it is specifically the modification indices that cause that error, just use the<font face=\"courier new, monospace\"> modificationIndices() </font>function.</div><div><br></div><div><div><div>Terrence D. Jorgensen</div><div>Postdoctoral Researcher, Methods and Statistics</div><div>Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam</div><div>UvA web page: <a href=\"http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792427591417000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0jRGPiy2yCEKMNRTG8dG-h\">http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen</a></div></div></div><div><br></div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
